# ImpactFeedAI — environment variables
#
# Copy to .env.local for local development:  cp .env.example .env.local
# Never commit real values. Every variable below is read directly by code in
# this repo (see docs/architecture.md for where each one is consumed).
#
# Next.js loads .env.local ahead of .env. The ingestion scripts run under tsx
# and load only .env via `dotenv/config` — if you keep both files, make sure
# DATABASE_URL matches in each or the app and the scripts will talk to
# different databases.


# ─── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required by: the web app (src/lib/prisma.ts), all Prisma CLI commands,
# and every ingestion/maintenance script.
# Postgres connection string. Local example:
#   postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/impactfeed
DATABASE_URL=""

# ─── Macro data sources (ingestion scripts only) ─────────────────────────────
# None of these are used by the running web app.

# Free key: https://fred.stlouisfed.org/docs/api/api_key.html
# Used by scripts/ingest/ for CPI / PPI / NFP / Fed funds release values and
# for the FOMC rate-decision walk. Without it the seed pipeline still runs
# (DataRelease rows fall back to hand-curated expected values), and
# auto-ingest skips its FRED and FOMC sources entirely.
FRED_API_KEY=""

# Optional. Free key: https://data.bls.gov/registrationEngine/
# Raises the BLS daily request cap from 25 to 500. scripts/ingest/sources-bls.ts
# works without it at low volume.
BLS_API_KEY=""
